    "LP BACnet"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Room panel (thermostat display)",
  "applies_to": "iSMA CONTROLLI iSMA-B-LP wall room panels with BACnet MS/TP firmware, with or without humidity and CO2 sensors.",
  "summary": "The iSMA-B-LP is an LCD room panel on BACnet MS/TP. It exposes its temperature, humidity and CO2 readings, a temperature setpoint with offset, fan mode and speed, and occupancy mode as objects, plus many display and keypad settings. Seven menus of user-defined numeric and boolean parameters let the BMS show and edit its own values on the panel.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "LP BACnet manual V1.2",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The manual table mixes objects and object properties. Only Present Value rows are listed as points; rows for other properties (offset, filter, limits, names, visibility, Device-object properties such as BACNET_DEVICE_ID and BAUD_RATE) are left out.",
    "AV 58 OFFSET_SETPOINT and MV 2 FAN_TYPE are printed with a property number (1503, 1602) instead of Present value; they are listed because the Touch Point manuals show them as Present value objects.",
    "DEFAULT_SETPOINT is printed as \"AC 57\"; it is listed as AV 57.",
    "The manual prints both OCCUPANCY_MODE and OCCUPANCY_CURRENT_STATUS as MV 4 (the Control Point manual puts the status on MV 3); both are kept as printed.",
    "User-defined parameter slots (NUMERIC1-8 as AV, BOOLEAN1-8 as BV) for the main menu and the temperature, fan, light, blind, alarm and occupancy submenus are all listed; the manual prints no MAINMENU_NUMERIC3 or NUMERIC7 row. Some slots are printed with clashing IDs: FAN_BOOLEAN1-8 as BV 8-15 (same as TEMPERATURE_BOOLEAN1-8), LIGHT_BOOLEAN1 as BV 31 (same as LIGHT_BOOLEAN8) and BLIND_NUMERIC1 as AV 31 (same as LIGHT_NUMERIC8). Those clashing rows are left out; the Control Point manual numbers the same slots fan BV 16-23, light BV 24-31 and blind AV 32-39."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "LP BACnet User Manual V1.2 - List of BACnet Objects",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": "V1.2",
    "url": "https://icdocs.ismacontrolli.com/lp-bacnet/V1.2/list-of-bacnet-objects"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Read the room temperature (AI 4), humidity (AI 5) and CO2 (AI 6) and the effective setpoint (AI 3); write the setpoint (AV 56), fan mode (MV 1) and occupancy mode (MV 4) when the BMS drives the room. BO 62 decides whether occupancy is local or set by the BMS.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "MV 4",
        "name": "OCCUPANCY_MODE",
        "why": "Occupancy mode, 1 = unoccupied, 2 = occupied"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 56",
        "name": "SETPOINT_VALUE",
        "why": "Temperature setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MV 1",
        "name": "FAN_MODE",
        "why": "Fan mode: 1 off, 2-4 manual speed, 5 auto"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "TEMPERATURE_SENSOR",
        "why": "Room temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 3",
        "name": "EFFECTIVE_SETPOINT",
        "why": "Effective setpoint (setpoint plus offset)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 5",
        "name": "HUMIDITY_SENSOR",
        "why": "Room humidity"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 6",
        "name": "CO2_SENSOR",
        "why": "Room CO2"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MV 0",
        "name": "FAN_CURRENT_SPEED",
        "why": "Current fan speed"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "BO 62 OCCUPIED_LOCAL_MODE selects local or BMS occupancy mode.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "Device instance and baud rate are Device-object properties (BACNET_DEVICE_ID default 0xFFFFFFFF, BAUD_RATE default 115200)."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Most configuration objects are stored in panel memory; avoid cyclic writes.",
      "Sensor objects exist only on panel versions with that sensor (MI 1 SENSORS gives the version)."
    ]
  },
